  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Gas oven took ages to light tonight then went WHOOMPH and now the kitchen smells really strongly of gas even though I've turned it off. Is it safe to try again?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "⚠ Stop using this appliance\nIf you can smell gas, treat it as an emergency: don't turn any switches on or off and no naked flames. Turn the gas off at the meter if you safely can, open doors and windows, and leave if the smell is strong. Call the National Gas Emergency line on 0800 111 999."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok I'm panicking a bit, the meter box is outside by the front door. should I go turn it off and open the windows? it's a rented place and I can't reach the landlord tonight. there's no CO alarm either"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "⚠ Stop using this appliance\nWhile you are out, open all doors and windows in the house to ventilate it. Do not try to use the oven again or attempt any repairs yourself; this is a serious safety issue that requires a Gas Safe engineer to inspect the ignition system and check for leaks before it is safe to use."
  }
